---
title: Numbers — Things 4 Good
description: The spreadsheet behind Things 4 Good — dollars raised, candles sold, transactions, payment mix, scent inventory, and candle math.
card:
  kicker: "Data lab"
  name: "The candle sale, counted carefully."
  summary: "Every fall we pour candles, track inventory, reconcile payments, chart what happened, and use the data to make the next sale better."
  photo: numbers
---
{% extends "base.njk" %}

{% block content %}
{% set ops = metrics.operations %}

<!-- ============================ HEADER ============================ -->
<section class="section section--ink page-head stats-hero" id="head">
  <div class="hero-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <a class="back-link" href="/">&larr; Things 4 Good</a>
    <p class="eyebrow">Data lab</p>
    <h1>The candle sale, counted carefully.</h1>
    <p class="lead">A fun thing about the fundraiser is that it lets us play the role of a retailer for a weekend. So we track inventory, reconcile payments and make a lot of charts, then use it all to make next year&rsquo;s sale better.</p>

    <div class="stats-hero-grid">
      <div class="stats-hero-total">
        <span>Raised since 2021</span>
        <b><span class="pre">$</span><span id="counter" data-target="{{ metrics.grandTotal }}">{{ metrics.grandTotalDisplay }}</span></b>
        <p>The candle sale, markets and little extras all count, and every dollar goes to the non-profits.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================ DASHBOARD ============================ -->
<section class="section" id="dashboard">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">The basics</p>
      <h2 class="t">The sale, by the numbers.</h2>
      <p class="lead">How many candles we&rsquo;ve sold, how many transactions that took, and what the spreadsheet says people actually did.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ops-grid">
      <div class="ops-card reveal"><div class="k">{{ ops.totals.candlesSoldDisplay }}</div><div class="l">Candles sold</div><p>Across five annual sales.</p></div>
      <div class="ops-card reveal"><div class="k">{{ ops.totals.transactions }}</div><div class="l">Transactions</div><p>Across five weekends of orders, preorders, pickup, and the occasional extra.</p></div>
      <div class="ops-card reveal"><div class="k">{{ ops.totals.avgCandlesPerTransaction }}</div><div class="l">Candles per transaction</div><p>Handy for figuring out how many vessels, how much wax and how much scent to order.</p></div>
      <div class="ops-card reveal"><div class="k">{{ ops.totals.venmoShareDisplay }}</div><div class="l">All-time Venmo share</div><p>{{ ops.totals.venmoCount }} of {{ ops.totals.paymentCount }} recorded payments.</p></div>
      <div class="ops-card reveal"><div class="k">{{ ops.latest.lidsSold }}</div><div class="l">Lids sold in {{ ops.latest.year }}</div><p>A new add-on that mostly helped gift purchases.</p></div>
      <div class="ops-card reveal"><div class="k">{{ ops.totals.latestLeft }}</div><div class="l">Candles left after {{ ops.latest.year }}</div><p>{{ ops.latest.candlesSold }} sold from {{ ops.latest.candlesMade }} prepared.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================ GROWTH ============================ -->
<section class="section section--paper2" id="growth">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Growth</p>
      <h2 class="t">It keeps growing, just not evenly.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Dollars raised have gone up every year, but candles and transactions each tell a slightly different story.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="year-grid reveal">
      {% for y in ops.years %}
      <a class="year-card" href="/impact/?event=candle-sale-{{ y.year }}" data-tinylytics-event="chart.year" data-tinylytics-event-value="{{ y.year }}">
        <div class="year-card-top">
          <span class="year-num">{{ y.year }}</span>
          <span class="year-chip">{{ y.growthDisplay }}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="year-card-metrics">
          <div><b>${{ y.raisedDisplay }}</b><span>raised</span></div>
          <div><b>{{ y.candlesSold }}</b><span>candles</span></div>
          <div><b>{{ y.transactions }}</b><span>transactions</span></div>
        </div>
        <p>{{ y.note }}</p>
      </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <div class="insight-row">
      <div class="insight reveal">
        <span class="k">Biggest dollar jump</span>
        <b>{{ (ops.years | last).growthDisplay }}</b>
        <p>{{ ops.latest.year }} raised ${{ ops.latest.raisedDisplay }}, even with fewer transactions than 2024.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="insight reveal">
        <span class="k">1,000th candle</span>
        <b>2025</b>
        <p>{{ ops.milestones[0].detail }}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================ HOW PEOPLE BUY ============================ -->
<section class="section" id="buying">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">How people buy</p>
      <h2 class="t">People tend to buy in pairs.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Order size is one of the most useful numbers for planning. It changes how much inventory we need, how checkout goes, how many bags and labels we use, and how much of a puzzle preorder pickup turns into.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="behavior-grid">
      <div class="histogram reveal">
        <div class="chart-title">
          <h3>{{ ops.latest.year }} order sizes</h3>
          <span>Candle transactions</span>
        </div>
        {% for d in ops.latestOrderDistribution %}
        <div class="hrow">
          <span>{{ d.candles }}</span>
          <i style="width:{{ d.barPct }}%"></i>
          <b>{{ d.transactions }}</b>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>

      <div class="payment-lab reveal">
        <div class="chart-title">
          <h3>Payment mix</h3>
          <span>{{ ops.latest.year }} recorded payments</span>
        </div>
        <div class="venmo-callout">
          <b>{{ ops.latest.venmoShareDisplay }}</b>
          <p>of recorded {{ ops.latest.year }} payments were Venmo.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pay-bars">
          {% for p in ops.latest.paymentMethods %}
          <div class="pay-row">
            <span>{{ p.method }}</span>
            <i style="width:{% if ops.latest.paymentTotal %}{{ (p.count / ops.latest.paymentTotal * 100) | round }}{% else %}0{% endif %}%"></i>
            <b>{{ p.count }}</b>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================ INVENTORY ============================ -->
<section class="section section--paper2" id="inventory">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Inventory</p>
      <h2 class="t">Scents are the hardest thing to predict.</h2>
      <p class="lead">In {{ ops.latest.year }} we added more products: Charcoal Rose, T4G Labs, Rekindled, XL candles and lids. This is where the sale starts to look like a tiny retail store.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="inventory-layout">
      <div class="scent-board reveal">
        <div class="chart-title">
          <h3>{{ ops.latest.year }} scent sell-through</h3>
          <span>{{ ops.latest.candlesSold }} sold &middot; {{ ops.latest.candlesMade }} prepared</span>
        </div>
        <div class="scent-grid">
        {% for scent in ops.latest.scents %}
        <div class="scent-card{% if scent.left == 0 %} sold-out{% endif %}{% if scent.left < 0 %} over-sold{% endif %}">
          <div class="scent-card-top">
            <h4>{{ scent.name }}</h4>
            <span>{{ scent.type }}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="scent-card-stats">
            <div><b>{{ scent.sold }}</b><span>sold</span></div>
            <div><b>{{ scent.made }}</b><span>made</span></div>
          </div>
          <p>{{ scent.leftDisplay }}</p>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="learn-card reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">What the data taught us</p>
        <h3>Adding more products completely broke our checkout!</h3>
        <p>XL candles, lids, T4G Labs and Rekindled made the sale more interesting, but our tracking sheets couldn&rsquo;t keep up. Jamie realized it on Saturday and <a href="https://www.thingelstad.com/2025/11/09/realized-we-had-some-big.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--marigold-d);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">redid them for Sunday</a>, and that was so much better.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><b>{{ ops.topLatestScent.sold }}</b> {{ ops.topLatestScent.name }} candles sold.</li>
          <li><b>{{ ops.latest.lidsSold }}</b> lids sold as a new add-on.</li>
          <li><b>{{ ops.totals.latestLeft }}</b> candles left after the sale.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================ CANDLE MATH ============================ -->
<section class="section" id="math">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Candle math</p>
      <h2 class="t">What {{ ops.totals.candlesSoldDisplay }} candles means in materials.</h2>
      <p class="lead">These are estimates based on what goes into one candle. They&rsquo;re useful for planning, not for non-profit accounting.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="math-grid">
      <div class="math-card reveal"><b>{{ ops.totals.waxLbs }} lbs</b><span>Wax melted and poured</span></div>
      <div class="math-card reveal"><b>{{ ops.totals.wickFt }} ft</b><span>Wooden wick set</span></div>
      <div class="math-card reveal"><b>{{ ops.totals.burnHrsDisplay }} hrs</b><span>Total burn time</span></div>
      <div class="math-card reveal"><b>${{ metrics.pricePerCandle }}</b><span>Base donation per 12 oz candle</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="cost-note reveal">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What it costs us</p>
        <h3>Each candle costs roughly {{ ops.materialCost.costRangeDisplay }} in materials.</h3>
        <p>{{ ops.materialCost.note }} When we catch sales and bulk discounts, the real range is closer to {{ ops.materialCost.discountRangeDisplay }}. We pay for that ourselves, so the full ${{ metrics.pricePerCandle }} donation goes to the non-profits.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="{{ ops.materialCost.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the cost post</a>
    </div>

    <p class="note-est reveal"><b>Good to know:</b> the dollars are what matter. The rest of this page is just us being nerds about candles. 🤓</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================ JOURNAL ============================ -->
<section class="section section--paper2" id="journal">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">From the blog</p>
      <h2 class="t">The charts have a backstory.</h2>
      <p class="lead">After each sale Jamie writes up the results, what surprised us and what the spreadsheets taught us.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="journal-grid">
      {% for post in metrics.journalPosts %}
      <a class="journal-card reveal" href="{{ post.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <span class="jtype">{{ post.type }} &middot; {{ post.year }}</span>
        <h4>{{ post.title }}</h4>
        <p>{{ post.description }}</p>
        <span class="go">Read post <span class="arr">&rarr;</span></span>
      </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="impact-link reveal"><a href="{{ site.blogUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Browse the full Things 4 Good blog category &rarr;</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================ CTA ============================ -->
<section class="section section--pine subscribe" id="cta">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow" style="justify-content:center">From numbers to names</p>
    <h2 class="t" style="max-width:20ch;margin-inline:auto">See where the money went.</h2>
    <p class="lead" style="margin:18px auto 0;text-align:center">This page is about how the sale works. The Impact page shows where every dollar went.</p>
    <div class="sub-form" style="max-width:none">
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/impact/">Explore the impact <span class="arr">&rarr;</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% endblock %}

{% block scripts %}
<script>
  const counter = document.getElementById('counter');
  const target = parseInt(counter.dataset.target, 10);
  const fmt = (n) => n.toLocaleString('en-US');
  let counted = false;
  const countIO = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
    entries.forEach((e) => {
      if (e.isIntersecting && !counted) {
        counted = true;
        const dur = 1400, t0 = performance.now();
        const tick = (now) => {
          const p = Math.min((now - t0) / dur, 1);
          const eased = 1 - Math.pow(1 - p, 3);
          counter.textContent = fmt(Math.round(target * eased));
          if (p < 1) requestAnimationFrame(tick);
        };
        requestAnimationFrame(tick);
      }
    });
  }, { threshold: 0.5 });
  countIO.observe(counter);
</script>
{% endblock %}
